<p>In the latest development in the sixth week of the Iran war, U.S. officials said American forces rescued the second crew member from an F-15E shot down over Iran, ending a tense search after the other crew member had already been recovered. President Trump said the rescued officer was injured but “will be just fine,” and multiple outlets said the mission involved special operations forces and heavy air support inside Iranian territory. The rescue offered a rare piece of good news amid a wider regional escalation. The F-15E was brought down on Friday during combat operations over Iran, and the search unfolded as Tehran and Washington traded new threats over the Strait of Hormuz and as strikes continued elsewhere in the region. Iranian media and officials also said their forces engaged U.S. aircraft during the rescue effort and claimed they hit additional American aircraft, though some of those claims had not been independently verified in other reporting.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/OVz-njxjksXu_tysV4i0_OGe1uahu2vbwIMyEi-p8TaqwKuLZyTjqyU4x25DqbptTghijw8A2Freq5_MO8edjU-AXmoX0GBlHBfBrUAnV-f5' alt='An F/A-18F Super Hornet prepares to launch from the flight deck of the US Navy Nimitz-class aircraft carrier USS Abraham Lincoln at an undisclosed location during the Operation Epic Fury attack on Iran on March 31, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Ground survival: The missing crew member, identified in several reports as the weapons systems officer, spent more than 24 hours on the ground after ejecting and was able to evade capture in mountainous terrain.</li><li>Earlier extraction under fire: Dawn reported that Iranian fire hit a U.S. Black Hawk used in the first recovery, wounding crew members before it returned to base.</li><li>Iranian hunt: Before the rescue was confirmed, Iranian calls to locate the “enemy pilot” included public appeals, a promised reward, and the deployment of local and paramilitary forces, according to PBS, NDTV and Politico.</li><li>Wider battlefield: Separate reporting said a strike near an Iranian nuclear power plant prompted evacuations, while the Israeli military detected another missile launch from Yemen as the rescue drama unfolded.</li><li>Firefight reports: NDTV and the South China Morning Post, citing other reporting, said the airman was located after a “heavy firefight,” suggesting the final recovery phase was contested on the ground as well as in the air.</li></ul><blockquote>WE GOT HIM! My fellow Americans, over the past several hours, the United States Military pulled off one of the most daring search and rescue operations in US history for one of our incredible crew member officers, who also happens to be a highly respected colonel, and who I am thrilled to let you know is now SAFE and SOUND! - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United States government: President Trump described the mission as an unusually difficult success, saying U.S. forces tracked the airman continuously and then sent dozens of aircraft to extract him after careful planning. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/trump-says-missing-us-crew-member-from-downed-jet-rescued/'>Politico</a>)</li><li>Iranian Revolutionary Guards: The Guards said Iranian forces destroyed several “enemy flying objects” during the rescue effort, part of Tehran’s push to show it contested the U.S. operation. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/iran-says-several-enemy-flying-objects-destroyed-during-us-pilot-rescue-mission'>Al-Monitor</a>)</li><li>Iranian military official: A senior Iranian military official rejected President Trump’s Hormuz ultimatum, calling it “a helpless, nervous, unbalanced and stupid action.” (<a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-us-trump-warns-more-coming-oil-gas-strait-hormuz/'>CBS News</a>)</li><li>Financial Times analysis: The rescue eased an immediate operational and political crisis for Washington, but the newspaper said it was unfolding inside a broader war that had already entered its sixth week and was still expanding geographically. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/764a9cda-eda0-4332-a4ce-6a26afaf7597'>Financial Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-war-us-says-missing-crew-member-from-downed-jet-found/live-76665046'>Iran war: US says missing crew member from downed jet found</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-rescues-airman-whose-f-15-was-downed-in-iran-say-us-officials/article70825889.ece'>U.S. rescues airman whose F-15 was downed in Iran, say U.S. officials</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/4/5/iran-war-live-tehran-rejects-trumps-ultimatum-fire-at-kuwait-oil-complex'>Iran war live: Trump confirms rescue of US officer, says ‘we got him’</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/637326-us-pilot-in-iran-saved/'>Missing pilot of downed fighter jet over Iran rescued – Trump</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/04/iran-says-several-enemy-flying-objects-destroyed-during-us-pilot-rescue-mission'>Iran says several &#x27;enemy flying objects&#x27; destroyed during US pilot rescue mission</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/764a9cda-eda0-4332-a4ce-6a26afaf7597'>US rescues second fighter jet airman shot down over Iran</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/inthenews/comments/1scu5jz/missing_us_crew_member_from_downed_fighter_jet/'>Missing U.S. crew member from downed fighter jet rescued in Iran, Trump says</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1988789/us-forces-rescue-2-airmen-downed-in-iran-trump-says-crew-member-injured-but-safe'>US forces rescue 2 airmen downed in Iran; Trump says crew member injured but ‘safe’</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/trump-says-missing-us-crew-member-from-downed-jet-rescued/'>US rescues m